Revision history for Game-Oware

0.04    2026-10-13
	- u and r, undo and redo, take back a turn and play it again
	- Add options, the fields a launcher offers before a game
	- The keys, the screen and the picker are Game::Terminal::Kit's
	- Requires perl 5.14
	- The moves in the picker are numbered
	- The picker is drawn over the last frame, with no clear between
	- to_text and from_text carry the variant, the first seat, the starting board, the seed, and a resignation, timeout or abandonment
	- Shift-tab moves the cursor back
	- Remove read_char, read_sequence and recent; add keyboard, screen,
	  log, last_move and picker

0.03    2026-10-11
	- Add Game::Oware::Terminal->run(@argv), which returns the exit status

0.02    2026-10-07
	- Pick a move with the arrow keys in the terminal, previewing the
	  position the move would produce.
	- The terminal board is drawn as a board: a store at each end, seed
	  clusters, colour, and a mark on every house the last move touched.
	- Fix: --ascii was a second glyph table identical to the first.
	- Fix: --quiet swallowed the result.
	- Fix: a command answered on the prompt's own line off a terminal.

0.01    2026-09-18
	First version
